course: dictionary
lesson: 2395
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Curry can be a food, a powder, or part of a phrase. Context tells you which meaning is right. Ask: what is the sentence about? «Ella ordered a mild chicken curry with rice.» Chicken and rice are the clues, so curry is a dish.
explain: «The curry stain on her shirt turned red when Sam washed it with soap.» A stain is a mark, so curry here must be the food that leaves a mark. Check by swapping in your meaning: a food stain makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Curry can also be part of a phrase. «Mia gave the teacher sweets every day to curry favour.» Gave sweets and to curry favour tell you Mia wants the teacher to like her. Here curry means to flatter someone so they like you. The phrase is what matters, not the single word.
fact: A curry is a dish of meat, fish or vegetables cooked in a spicy sauce.
fact: Curry is often eaten with rice or bread, and it comes from South Asian cooking.
fact: Curry powder is a mixture of spices used to make curry dishes.
fact: To curry favour means to flatter someone or do things for them so they will like you.
fact: A curry can be mild or very hot. «Yellow turmeric turns reddish-brown with an alkali, so a curry stain can turn red when washed with soap.»
exercise: «Ella ordered a mild chicken curry with rice.» What is a curry in this sentence? | *A dish of meat or vegetables in a spicy sauce | A kind of rice pudding | A type of bread baked in an oven | A sweet drink made with milk
exercise: «The curry stain on her shirt turned red when Sam washed it with soap.» What is the curry here? | A bright yellow paint | *Food that leaves a mark, such as a spicy sauce | A pair of socks | A shiny metal bowl
exercise: «Mia gave the teacher sweets every day to curry favour.» What does curry favour mean? | To cook a spicy dinner for the teacher | To wash the teacher's car | *To flatter someone so they will like you | To shout loudly in class
test: «Ravi sprinkled curry powder over the rice.» What is curry powder? | A dried leaf used to make tea | A pudding made with sugar and milk | *A mixture of spices used to make curry dishes
test: Which phrase means to flatter someone to make them like you? | Curry powder | Curry stain | *Curry favour | Chicken curry
exam: «We ate a very hot curry, and Dad drank a whole glass of water.» What does hot mean here? | Stolen | Hot-tempered and angry | *Very spicy | Warm to touch
